# Step 188D: backend Docker build-context cleanup
# (docs/14_backend_architecture.md section 129). Every pattern below
# keeps a local/dev/runtime artifact out of both the Docker build
# context sent to the daemon and the final image -- none of this
# removes the file from the real backend/ directory on disk, and none
# of it is a claim that the resulting image is "production-ready".
# `alembic/`, `alembic.ini`, and `requirements.txt` are deliberately
# NEVER excluded here -- see the `app/tests/` note below and
# docs/14_backend_architecture.md section 129 for the full reasoning.

# Local persisted state / caches (backend/.data/ -- the gitignored
# LocalJsonStore JSON file, provider_cache.sqlite3, manual-scrape HTML
# fixtures, and any in-progress atomic-write .tmp file). Never safe to
# bake into an image: it's per-developer/per-machine local state, not
# application code, and baking it in would make every build
# non-reproducible and could leak one developer's local trip data into
# an image built from their machine.
.data/

# Python bytecode/caches
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Build artifacts -- no backend build step produces these today;
# excluded defensively for consistency with common Python project
# layouts, not because any of them currently exist here.
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# OS/editor cruft
.DS_Store

# Virtualenvs -- never needed inside the image; the Dockerfile installs
# requirements.txt directly into the image's own Python interpreter.
.venv/
venv/

# Logs -- this app logs to stdout only (see
# docs/14_backend_architecture.md section 121); nothing writes a log
# file today, excluded defensively.
logs/
*.log

# Real secrets -- never committed to this repo, excluded defensively.
# See .env.example for the safe, secret-free template that IS meant to
# be read (by a human, not copied into a Docker build).
.env
.env.*

# Step 188D: the backend test suite. Excluded from the build context/
# image because nothing in this runtime image ever runs pytest --
# requirements-dev.txt (the only place pytest is declared) is already
# never installed into this image (see backend/Dockerfile), and no
# runtime code path imports anything under app/tests/ (confirmed by
# grep across app/ and scripts/ before adding this line). Tests still
# run exactly as before -- on the host (`pytest` from the repo root)
# and in CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) -- neither of which reads this
# file or runs inside a container's built image. If a later step adds
# a CI job that runs tests *inside* a container, that job would need
# its own build (or a bind-mounted source tree, the way
# docker-compose.yml's dev `backend` service already mounts
# `./backend:/app`) rather than relying on this runtime image
# containing app/tests/.
app/tests/
